From: =?UTF-8?q?L=C3=A9onard?= <leonard@synthe.se>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 10:46:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] ata: libahci: Warn about masking port_map only when ports
 are masked

On platform AHCI controllers, ahci_platform_get_resources() sets
mask_port_map to the ports that have an enabled child node in the device
tree. A device tree that describes every port of the controller then
triggers the warning although nothing is masked, as on the BCM7231:

  masking port_map 0x3 -> 0x3

Keep applying the mask, but warn only when it actually drops a port.
---
 drivers/ata/libahci.c | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/ata/libahci.c b/drivers/ata/libahci.c
index 08ab56e..645c16e 100644
--- a/drivers/ata/libahci.c
+++ b/drivers/ata/libahci.c
@@ -544,9 +544,10 @@ void ahci_save_initial_config(struct device *dev, struct ahci_host_priv *hpriv)
 
 	/* mask_port_map not set means that all ports are available */
 	if (hpriv->mask_port_map) {
-		dev_warn(dev, "masking port_map 0x%lx -> 0x%lx\n",
-			port_map,
-			port_map & hpriv->mask_port_map);
+		if (port_map & ~hpriv->mask_port_map)
+			dev_warn(dev, "masking port_map 0x%lx -> 0x%lx\n",
+				 port_map,
+				 port_map & hpriv->mask_port_map);
 		port_map &= hpriv->mask_port_map;
 	}
 
